Z||000001||kornholio||09-20-1999||08:10 PM||||I'd also like some info on these mufflers also.  How much different does it sound from the stock muffler?  And which series should I buy?  I'd like to be noticed, but not pulled over.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-20-1999||08:44 PM||||My brother and I both have the big case flowmasters on v8's and agree that they are too loud. I can't say how one might sound on a 2.5, but it may be a bit much- especially if you don't have a cat converter. ||||reg||4
Z||000003||Bruce||09-20-1999||11:49 PM||||When checking through the forum for the Flowmaster part # replacement muffler for the V6, the model is the 80 series. I haven't had mine installed yet, so I'm interested to hear the results of anyone who has done this particular part replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||09-22-1999||09:59 PM||||well guys i went to the muffler shop and it's true, they don't like doing fiero's. so now i have to put it in myself, i'll let you guys know how it went,and how it sounds. ||||reg||13
Z||000005||Racer 1||09-23-1999||01:49 AM||||Awhile back I chunked that piece of junk muffle the fiero came with. I put straight pipe out the back with resonator pencil tips. Wow what a big improvment in performance in the 2.5 iron ducky engine. Then just a week ago I had a muffle shop put on a 12" glasspack with a single 3" pencil tip going out the passenger side rear. This setup gave me more mid range punch but not as much on top rush. I rapped my exhaust stuff in 2" header rap this cuts down on the temp under the hood with my HOOKER super comp headers by about 100 degrees or more.||||reg||14
